.TH AIUSAGEMONITOR 1 "2026" "aiusagemonitor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aiusagemonitor \- live TUI usage/limit monitor for OpenAI, Claude, Google Gemini and xAI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aiusagemonitor
[\fIflags\fR]
.br
.B aiusagemonitor
\fIcommand\fR [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aiusagemonitor
is a terminal UI that shows live token usage, rate limits, cost and
historic statistics for the major AI vendor APIs. It gathers data by
tailing local AI coding-assistant session logs (Claude Code, Codex CLI,
Gemini CLI), through a built-in local capture proxy, or by polling a
vendor's usage/admin API, and persists everything to a local SQLite
database for historic summaries and usage profiling.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
(none)
Launch the interactive TUI. This is the default when no subcommand is given.
.TP
.B report
Print a text or JSON usage summary for a time range and exit. Useful in
scripts, cron jobs or a status bar.
.TP
.B proxy
Run the capture proxy headlessly (no TUI), logging status to stdout.
.TP
.B paths
Print the resolved config file and database paths.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FLAGS (TUI)
.TP
.B \-config \fIPATH\fR
Config file path (default: \fI~/.config/aiusagemonitor/config.yaml\fR).
.TP
.B \-db \fIPATH\fR
History database path (overrides the config file).
.TP
.B \-demo
Clean showcase mode: only synthetic traffic is shown, every real collector
is disabled for the run.
.TP
.B \-theme \fINAME\fR
Start with the given theme.
.TP
.B \-no-mouse
Disable mouse reporting.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B tab / shift+tab
Next / previous view.
.TP
.B 1-6
Jump directly to a view.
.TP
.B t / T
Next / previous theme.
.TP
.B p
Pause / resume live updates.
.TP
.B r
Force an immediate refresh.
.TP
.B ?
Open the Help view.
.TP
.B q, ctrl+c
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/aiusagemonitor/config.yaml
Configuration, including provider connection settings. Written with 0600
permissions since it may hold API keys.
.TP
.I ~/.config/aiusagemonitor/history.db
SQLite history database.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation: https://github.com/kawaiipantsu/aiusagemonitor
